Body:
Still actively maintained, and the automated review feedback has been addressed since this was opened:
- notebook parsing now uses a safe YAML schema (`CORE_SCHEMA`) so hostile JS tags can't be instantiated, with a regression test;
- the shared save-learnings prompt is centralized instead of hardcoded inline;
- the mid-task note attach is opt-out via `experimental.notebook.attach`.
Typecheck and tests pass. This is the core of the per-folder notebook memory proposal in #43068. Could a maintainer please reopen it for human review?
